Find the moment of inertia of this lamina about the $y$-axis." 13194139535742 true] [17592186364362 1113 #uuid "567c1d0c-a247-52c4-bf76-77c7361081f4" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364362 1145 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}y]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4+\\frac{8y}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[4y+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =12+12 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $y$-axis is $24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364363 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364364 13194139535742 true] [17592186364363 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364365 13194139535742 true] [17592186364363 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364366 13194139535742 true] [17592186364363 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364367 13194139535742 true] [17592186364363 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364368 13194139535742 true] [17592186364363 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535742 true] [17592186364363 1041 "selection" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364363 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364368 13194139535742 true] [17592186364363 1110 #uuid "bc0c365a-dbfe-57ac-a777-1d559f1db0e7" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364364 1034 "16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" 1