e that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/dd5ee021dd73317a775c0ea653212f7ee5545f8c6854e6a9daabdc93b5c3b9c0.png)\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot 3y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}3{x}^{2}y+3{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{3}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3}+\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{8}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =96+16 \\\\  & =112.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364378 13194139535742 true] [17592186364377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364379 13194139535742 true] [17592186364377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364380 13194139535742 true] [17592186364377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364381 13194139535742 true] [17592186364377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364382 13194139535742 true] [17592186364377 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535742 true] [17592186364377 1041 "selection" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364377 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364380 13194139535742 true] [17592186364377 1110 #uuid "ab77f835-d061-575b-91fa-5ebec5fb210e" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364378 1034 "66" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364378 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364378 1111 #uuid "ce215896-0628-504b-b6c2-51ecc21f5b3a" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364379 1034 "88" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364379 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364379 1111 #uuid "1676c11d-0acd-5884-b7e3-089cf89e933b" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364380 1034 "112" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364380 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364380 1111 #uuid "09c0fa76-d163-5cda-92bb-73991ff8b828" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364381 1034 "96" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364381 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364381 1111 #uuid "b579d07c-e4eb-5d46-8f45-12a7c3432faa" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364382 1034 "124" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364382 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364382 1111 #uuid "1bb18832-4b39-594d-b940-8af02a8390d1" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364383 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364384 13194139535742 true] [17592186364383 1089 "q-163180" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364383 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535742 true] [17592186364383 1100 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis.\nFind the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $y$-axis." 13194139535742 true] [17592186364383 1113 #uuid "a8bb967c-3713-5f4d-a731-98f880cc76f8" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364383 1145 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k|y|=ky,\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}ky\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k[x]_{0}^{3}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =k(3-0)(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3k}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\frac{2M}{3}$ and hence,\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=ky=\\frac{2M}{3}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{3}({\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{3}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{3}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{3}(9-0)(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364384 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364385 13194139535742 true] [17592186364384 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364386 13194139535742 true] [17592186364384 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364387 13194139535742 true] [17592186364384 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364388 13194139535742 true] [17592186364384 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364389 13194139535742 true] [17592186364384 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535742 true] [17592186364384 1041 "selection" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364384 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364387 13194139535742 true] [17592186364384 1110 #uuid "eb2c7b68-a5b3-5920-aa62-d8a781ac907a" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364385 1034 "\\frac{M}{2}" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364385 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364385 1111 #uuid "d6aa7e02-f624-574e-bb4e-88134b2affc3" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364386 1034 "M" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364386 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364386 1111 #uuid "5a0b84bc-628a-5173-906c-44830a8aee5a" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364387 1034 "3M" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364387 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364387 1111 #uuid 