-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/626cbf8e182d9eebb8b48026f07c5dd012c1096cc9568465f3648710ea0d07a4.png)\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})(10y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}10{x}^{2}y+10{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[5{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{5}{2}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}5{x}^{2}(4-{x}^{2})+\\frac{5}{2}{(4-{x}^{2})}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{2}(4-{x}^{2})(2{x}^{2}+4-{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}16-{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{[16x-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(32-\\frac{32}{5}) \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364392 13194139535742 true] [17592186364391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364393 13194139535742 true] [17592186364391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364394 13194139535742 true] [17592186364391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364395 13194139535742 true] [17592186364391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364396 13194139535742 true] [17592186364391 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535742 true] [17592186364391 1041 "selection" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364391 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364392 13194139535742 true] [17592186364391 1110 #uuid "51723526-c4a3-5890-b64c-fee18c254140" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364392 1034 "64" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364392 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364392 1111 #uuid "7dabfa54-9e3c-58d8-82f8-1c95511706dd" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364393 1034 "50" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364393 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364393 1111 #uuid "8e90fbcf-fcbb-5e76-a8d1-5677776f1a48" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364394 1034 "58" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364394 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364394 1111 #uuid "0d7055ee-c8cf-540a-a1bc-012444b8e4be" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364395 1034 "72" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364395 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364395 1111 #uuid "cae28922-3f15-53ec-a4df-1e27139d3f43" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364396 1034 "49" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364396 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364396 1111 #uuid "1b495bc3-cfae-516f-a9db-c89e4c622cf2" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364397 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364398 13194139535742 true] [17592186364397 1089 "q-163186" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364397 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535742 true] [17592186364397 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/043119a0637985fa55a7084a8d4b67df5031b24211ab421ec019700235ca2365.png)\n\nA triangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant enclosed by the line $y=1-x$ and the coordinate axes. The mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $x$-axis." 13194139535742 true] [17592186364397 1113 #uuid "62c73ee4-534d-5429-b48c-9e2202076205" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364397 1145 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/782b4df0220d84d90d26a4ad1fd4a34da00ecf3c5d62a9416d9f0490ca765e2b.png)\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}k{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}(1-x)^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{3}{[-\\frac{1}{4}(1-x)^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=12M$ and hence $\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2}=12M{y}^{2}.$ Therefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{y}^{2}({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{5}{y}^{5}]}_{0}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{5}(1-x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}{[-\\frac{1}{6}(1-x)^{6}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364399 13194139535742 true] [17592186364398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364400 13194139535742 true] [17592186364398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364401 13194139535742 true] [17592186364398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364402 13194139535742 true] [17592186364398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364403 13194139535742 true] [17592186364398 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535742 true] [17592186364398 1041 "selectio