2" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364404 1145 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/f08ac68e3d8992e70cdc40eddfb9cdc39ee16a275890f3d9d7db42a682866bf6.png)\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}k{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[{x}^{2}y]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\frac{M}{4}$ and hence,\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2}=\\frac{M}{4}{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[{x}^{4}y]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{4}(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{[\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{6}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}\\cdot \\frac{32}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364406 13194139535742 true] [17592186364405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364407 13194139535742 true] [17592186364405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364408 13194139535742 true] [17592186364405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364409 13194139535742 true] [17592186364405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364410 13194139535742 true] [17592186364405 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535742 true] [17592186364405 1041 "selection" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364405 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364408 13194139535742 true] [17592186364405 1110 #uuid "55f4bfc2-50a7-54e6-af10-d51346698c9a" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364406 1034 "6M" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364406 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364406 1111 #uuid "02e6630c-651d-5a2c-b421-84ec3f775f36" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364407 1034 "4M" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364407 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364407 1111 #uuid "2f79fbf5-ceb2-58cb-b025-5d89e2b58594" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364408 1034 "\\frac{8M}{3}" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364408 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364408 1111 #uuid "e9883c73-3b5e-5e84-a8d6-41d516bb16a0" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364409 1034 "\\frac{7M}{6}" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364409 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364409 1111 #uuid "1a6dec5d-8904-5e76-b332-526199c33536" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364410 1034 "\\frac{2M}{3}" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364410 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364410 1111 #uuid "69cf6182-90b0-56b9-8e61-b2bf21564f81" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364411 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364412 13194139535742 true] [17592186364411 1089 "q-163200" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364411 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535742 true] [17592186364411 1100 "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 4},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the origin." 13194139535742 true] [17592186364411 1113 #uuid "bdbe5d34-53d8-5fa8-ab86-b773c4a96924" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364411 1145 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 3=9.$ \n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{9}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{1}^{4}9+3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{[9y+{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}(36+64-9-1) \\\\  & =10M\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $10M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364412 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364413 13194139535742 true] [17