 $x$-axis and the lines $y=3x$ and $y=4-x,$ as shown above. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $x$-axis." 13194139535742 true] [17592186364425 1113 #uuid "79941e95-b786-504a-89df-1f073b7dd438" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364425 1145 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type II region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,\\frac{y}{3}\\le x\\le 4-y},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/47c897bd58a23965d9c36f683553c0817afa8bc2e37ed53a432edcd62b386e55.png)\n\nThe area of the triangular plate $D$ is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{y/3}^{4-y}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{y/3}^{4-y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}(4-y-\\frac{1}{3}y)\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{y}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{[\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{4}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(36-27) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364427 13194139535742 true] [17592186364426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364428 13194139535742 true] [17592186364426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364429 13194139535742 true] [17592186364426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364430 13194139535742 true] [17592186364426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364431 13194139535742 true] [17592186364426 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535742 true] [17592186364426 1041 "selection" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364426 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364428 13194139535742 true] [17592186364426 1110 #uuid "6d7449fa-6802-5070-99f2-2c2cd1437003" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364427 1034 "\\frac{M}{2}" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364427 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364427 1111 #uuid "cbb20b5a-b47c-5eb6-81c2-91d3970ea90c" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364428 1034 "\\frac{3M}{2}" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364428 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364428 1111 #uuid "413ef5e7-06b3-55df-a5f0-694083b4c0f0" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364429 1034 "3M" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364429 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364429 1111 #uuid "f47f5895-e52d-5cb1-a5a4-2aae43678d8e" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364430 1034 "2M" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364430 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364430 1111 #uuid "d3df9fb8-d934-55c9-bb4b-7236aaa66940" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364431 1034 "\\frac{M}{3}" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364431 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535742 true] [17592186364431 1111 #uuid "aa3544b6-e032-526f-a164-ef74ea80aabf" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364432 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364433 13194139535742 true] [17592186364432 1089 "q-163219" 13194139535742 true] [17592186364432 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535742 true] [17592186364432 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/140